# This repository is public. Track only what is certainly meant to be public.
#
# Listing what to leave out fails open: a new tool drops a new file and the default is
# "tracked", and what lands in history is hard to take back out. So the sections below
# are broad, and anything meant for readers has a named home.

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 1. Secrets. A value committed once is a value to treat as burned.
#    Nothing in this repository needs a secret: it runs offline and holds no funds.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
*.jks
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
credentials.json
secrets.json
*.wallet.json

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 2. Working notes. Anything meant for readers goes under docs/public/.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/docs/*
!/docs/public/
*.local.md
/scratch/
/sandbox/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
*.rej

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 3. Rust. Narrowed from github/gitignore's template: its bare `debug` and `target`
#    match a directory of that name anywhere, so a future `src/debug/` module would
#    disappear without a word. Cargo.lock is tracked on purpose — this workspace
#    ships a binary, and a proof system pinned today should build the same tomorrow.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/target/
**/target/
/debug/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb
**/mutants.out*/
*.crate
/flamegraph.svg
/perf.data*

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 4. What running the proof systems leaves behind.
#    Parameters, proving keys and ceremony transcripts are generated on the reader's
#    machine. They are large, and a published one would invite people to trust it.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#    Only the two directories a development run writes to, and the two ceremony formats
#    other tools produce — a wider pattern would silently drop a test fixture.
/params/
/runs/
*.ptau
*.zkey

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 5. Things checking the work leaves behind. Only files dropped at the root, so an
#    image a document ships with is never swallowed in silence.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.webp
/*.svg
*.log

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# 6. What machines and editors leave lying around.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/
.zed/
.fleet/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
